Post-verification feedback on your previous Rust:
Conformance violation at event 0: observed mutex_lock:main::m, expected one of []. You introduced a synchronization operation the design does not have. A CIR `var` must live inside the mutex that protects it, not behind a new lock, and `main` must not add shared-state access. [detail: no model statement matches mutex_lock on "main::m" (thread t1)]
Fix the Rust; do not change the design.

